Oolite original OOJSScript UTF-16 source loader native qualification
Date: 2026-11-19
Lab: team1-oolite-jsapi-rc1-20261119
Target: AC090 native AmigaOS 68040, GCC 16.2.0-open3
Executable SHA256: 465643b0d8c36ec28e4a0075b41d0d7424a229a3426312aa982888005b44cc3d
Source: src/Core/OOGFOSScriptObjects.c OOGFOSScriptObjectLoadUTF16

Original Oolite JS_CompileUCScript receives NSString utf16DataWithBOM:NO
(native-endian 16-bit units). Canonical GFOS JS_Evaluate receives UTF-8.
The new loader validates the code units, converts both BMP and valid
surrogate pairs to UTF-8, rejects malformed sequences and embedded zero,
then passes the script to the existing per-script-this execution seam.

Verbatim ACAgent native guest output:
OOLITE_JS_UTF16_SUITE_BEGIN
OOLITE_JS_UTF16 posted=0 valid=0 malformed=4 nul=4 low=4 called=1 result=42 status=PASS
OOLITE_JS_UTF16_RC 0
OOLITE_JS_UTF16_SUITE_END

The resulting script's event method sees note.length==3 containing U+00E9
and the UTF-16 pair U+D83D U+DE80 (U+1F680), and returns 42.
JSERR_BADARGS=4 is observed for an unmatched high surrogate, embedded
NUL, and unmatched low surrogate. Test executes in the JS task.
This validates the encoding boundary, not all original OOJSScript loading,
manifest properties, XDR cached scripts or full game operation.
